+# UsdtYieldVault — pre-deployment review
+
+**Verdict: do not ship this on Monday.** The vault as it stands cannot take a single
+deposit on mainnet — `deposit()` reverts against the real USDT contract, every time,
+for everyone. Behind that first wall there are four further defects, two of which lose
+user money on the happy path.
+
+Nothing under `src/` was changed. All new tests live in `test/audit/`;
+`test/UsdtYieldVault.t.sol` and `test/mocks/` are untouched and still pass 39/39.
+
+---
+
+## Why the green tick proved nothing
+
+The existing suite is green and covers 100% of lines and functions:
+
+```
+$ forge coverage --match-path 'test/UsdtYieldVault.t.sol' --no-match-coverage 'test/'
+...
+Ran 1 test suite in 11.52ms (7.16ms CPU time): 39 tests passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped (39 total tests)
+
+╭------------------------+-----------------+----------------+--------------+-----------------╮
+| File                   | % Lines         | % Statements   | % Branches   | % Funcs         |
++============================================================================================+
+| src/UsdtYieldVault.sol | 100.00% (52/52) | 98.25% (56/57) | 85.71% (6/7) | 100.00% (11/11) |
+|------------------------+-----------------+----------------+--------------+-----------------|
+| Total                  | 100.00% (52/52) | 98.25% (56/57) | 85.71% (6/7) | 100.00% (11/11) |
+╰------------------------+-----------------+----------------+--------------+-----------------╯
+```
+
+Coverage records which lines ran. It never records whether an assertion *could* have
+failed. Concretely, in the 39 tests:
+
+* **13 of them assert the implementation back to itself** and constrain nothing:
+  `test_ConstructorSetsUsdt`, `…SetsAUsdt`, `…SetsAavePool`, `…SetsOwner`,
+  `…SetsDepositFee` (constructor state vs. the constructor argument),
+  `test_BpsDenominator`, `test_ShareScale`, `test_MinDeposit`, `test_WithdrawFeeBps`
+  (a constant vs. itself), `test_SetDepositFeeUpdatesValue` (a getter vs. the value
+  just written), plus `test_SharePriceAfterDeposit`, `test_ConvertToSharesAfterDeposit`,
+  `test_ConvertToAssetsAfterDeposit`, which only assert `> 0`.
+* **Every test runs against `MockUSDT`**, a stock OpenZeppelin ERC20. Real USDT is not
+  one. A mock encodes the assumption; re-running it 39 times re-tests the assumption,
+  never the token. This is how finding **F1** — a total deposit failure on mainnet —
+  survived to sign-off.
+* **`MockAToken` never accrues.** It mints 1:1 and sits there. Real aUSDT rebases. That
+  is how **F2** survived.
+* **Every test exercises one or two operations in isolation.** Nothing states a property
+  over a *sequence*, so the accounting drift in **F3** — which is invisible after any
+  single withdrawal and grows with each one — had nowhere to show up.
+
+Static analysis adds nothing here either; it is clean on high/medium:
+
+```
+$ slither . --filter-paths "lib/|test/" --exclude-informational --exclude-low
+'forge clean' running (wd: .../testing-goal-001)
+'forge config --json' running
+'forge build --build-info --deny never --skip ./test/** ./script/** --force' running (wd: .../testing-goal-001)
+INFO:Slither:. analyzed (14 contracts with 64 detectors), 0 result(s) found
+```
+
+All five findings below came from the three searches the suite never performed: a
+domain fuzz of the owner-settable fee, a handler-driven invariant tying accounting to
+custody, and a pinned mainnet fork against the real USDT and the real Aave V3 pool.
+
+---
+
+## F1 — CRITICAL: `deposit()` reverts on mainnet. The vault is inoperable.
+
+`deposit()` calls `usdt.approve(address(aavePool), amount)` through the `IERC20`
+interface (`src/UsdtYieldVault.sol:94`). Real USDT's `approve` returns **no data**.
+Solidity's high-level call decodes a `bool` from a zero-length return buffer and
+reverts. The vault already uses `SafeERC20` for `safeTransferFrom` two lines above —
+the `approve` was simply missed.
+
+Note the shape of this bug: the state change *succeeds* (the `Approval` event is
+emitted), then the whole frame reverts on the return decode. No amount of mock-based
+testing reaches it, because `MockUSDT` returns a bool.
+
+**Evidence** (pinned fork, block 21,000,000, real USDT + real Aave V3 pool):
+
+```
+$ forge test --match-test test_DepositRevertsAgainstRealUsdt -vvvv
+  [94204] MainnetForkTest::test_DepositRevertsAgainstRealUsdt()
+    ├─ [0] VM::prank(alice: [0x328809Bc894f92807417D2dAD6b7C998c1aFdac6])
+    │   └─ ← [Return]
+    ├─ [84174] UsdtYieldVault::deposit(1000000000 [1e9])
+    │   ├─ [43630] 0xdAC17F958D2ee523a2206206994597C13D831ec7::transferFrom(alice: [0x328809Bc894f92807417D2dAD6b7C998c1aFdac6], UsdtYieldVault: [0x5615dEB798BB3E4dFa0139dFa1b3D433Cc23b72f], 1000000000 [1e9])
+    │   │   ├─ emit Transfer(from: alice: [0x328809Bc894f92807417D2dAD6b7C998c1aFdac6], to: UsdtYieldVault: [0x5615dEB798BB3E4dFa0139dFa1b3D433Cc23b72f], value: 1000000000 [1e9])
+    │   │   └─ ← [Stop]
+    │   ├─ [24953] 0xdAC17F958D2ee523a2206206994597C13D831ec7::approve(0x87870Bca3F3fD6335C3F4ce8392D69350B4fA4E2, 1000000000 [1e9])
+    │   │   ├─ emit Approval(owner: UsdtYieldVault: [0x5615dEB798BB3E4dFa0139dFa1b3D433Cc23b72f], spender: 0x87870Bca3F3fD6335C3F4ce8392D69350B4fA4E2, value: 1000000000 [1e9])
+    │   │   └─ ← [Stop]
+    │   └─ ← [Revert] EvmError: Revert
+    └─ ← [Revert] EvmError: Revert
+
+Backtrace:
+  at UsdtYieldVault.deposit
+  at MainnetForkTest.test_DepositRevertsAgainstRealUsdt
+
+Suite result: FAILED. 0 passed; 1 failed; 0 skipped; finished in 366.66ms (360.67µs CPU time)
+```
+
+The control pair in the same file isolates the cause to the return decode, not to
+permissions or balances: `test_Control_RawApproveOnRealUsdtReverts` fails, while the
+same call made low-level succeeds and returns 0 bytes
+(`approve() returndata length: 0`, see the F2 evidence block).
+
+**Fix:** use `usdt.forceApprove(address(aavePool), amount)` from `SafeERC20` (it both
+tolerates the missing return value and handles USDT's non-zero→non-zero approval
+restriction). Better still, approve the pool once for `type(uint256).max` in the
+constructor, or reset to 0 after the `supply` call so no standing allowance is left.
+
+---
+
+## F2 — CRITICAL: Aave yield never reaches depositors; a one-year holder loses money.
+
+`totalAssetsStored` is a plain counter that only moves on deposit and withdraw.
+`totalAssets()` returns it verbatim. The vault's actual position is a *rebasing* aUSDT
+balance that grows every second — and the `aUsdt` immutable, despite being stored, is
+never read anywhere in the contract. So the interest is earned, and then never
+attributed to anyone: share price is frozen, `balanceOfUnderlying` is frozen, and a
+depositor redeems principal minus the 0.3% withdrawal fee no matter how long they stay.
+
+This is not a rounding issue. It is the entire product premise failing silently.
+
+**Evidence** (pinned fork, block 21,000,000; real USDT, real Aave pool, real aUSDT
+accrual over 365 days at the rate live at that block). The unsafe `approve` of F1 is
+neutralised at the *test* boundary only — the allowance is granted for real first, then
+`approve` is stubbed so the return decode no longer reverts. The `transferFrom`, the
+`supply`, the aUSDT accrual and the `withdraw` are all real, unmocked mainnet calls:
+
+```
+$ forge test --match-path 'test/audit/MainnetFork.t.sol' -vv
+No files changed, compilation skipped
+
+Ran 5 tests for test/audit/MainnetFork.t.sol:MainnetForkTest
+[FAIL: totalAssets() must track the aUSDT the vault actually holds: 100000000000 != 104256651917] test_AaveYieldNeverReachesDepositors() (gas: 363932)
+Logs:
+  aUSDT held at deposit        : 100000000000
+  aUSDT held after 365 days    : 104256651917
+  interest actually earned     : 4256651917
+  totalAssets() after 365 days : 100000000000
+  alice balanceOfUnderlying    : 100000000000
+  sharePrice at deposit        : 1001001
+  sharePrice after 365 days    : 1001001
+
+[PASS] test_Control_LowLevelApproveOnRealUsdtSucceedsAndReturnsNoData() (gas: 37430)
+Logs:
+  approve() returndata length: 0
+
+[FAIL: EvmError: Revert] test_Control_RawApproveOnRealUsdtReverts() (gas: 35103)
+[FAIL: EvmError: Revert] test_DepositRevertsAgainstRealUsdt() (gas: 94204)
+[FAIL: a yield vault must not return less than the principal after a year: 99700000000 < 100000000000] test_SoleDepositorLosesMoneyOverAYearOfYield() (gas: 413443)
+Logs:
+  alice deposited              : 100000000000
+  alice received back          : 99700000000
+  aUSDT left stranded in vault : 4556651917
+  shares outstanding           : 0
+
+Suite result: FAILED. 1 passed; 4 failed; 0 skipped; finished in 219.06ms (2.90ms CPU time)
+```
+
+Read the numbers: on 100,000 USDT the vault earned **4,256.65 USDT** of real Aave
+interest in a year. `totalAssets()` still reported 100,000.000000 and `sharePrice()` was
+bit-for-bit unchanged at 1001001. The sole depositor withdrew everything and got
+**99,700 USDT back for 100,000 in** — a 300 USDT loss — while **4,556.65 USDT** sat in
+the vault's aUSDT balance with zero shares outstanding and no function able to reach it.
+
+**Fix:** delete `totalAssetsStored` and derive `totalAssets()` from the live position:
+`return aUsdt.balanceOf(address(this));`. aUSDT's `balanceOf` already includes accrued
+interest, so share price then rises with yield automatically and both conversion
+functions become correct without further change. If you want to keep a stored counter
+for gas reasons, you must add a `harvest()` that credits
+`aUsdt.balanceOf(this) - totalAssetsStored` before any share-price-sensitive operation —
+strictly worse and easy to get wrong. Derive it.
+
+---
+
+## F3 — HIGH: the withdrawal fee is destroyed, not distributed, and the gap compounds.
+
+`withdraw()` subtracts the **gross** amount from accounting but only pulls the **net**
+out of Aave (`src/UsdtYieldVault.sol:117-119`):
+
+```solidity
+totalAssetsStored -= grossAssets;
+aavePool.withdraw(address(usdt), netAssets, msg.sender);
+```
+
+So after each withdrawal the vault holds `fee` more aUSDT than it believes it holds. The
+contract's own NatSpec claims "Both fees stay supplied in Aave and accrue to the
+remaining shareholders" — for the deposit fee that is true, for the withdrawal fee it is
+false. Because the fee is removed from `totalAssetsStored`, it never lifts the share
+price. It is simply orphaned. Note that a one-sided solvency check (`claims <= holdings`)
+would stay green through all of this: the vault holds a *surplus*, not a shortfall.
+The property has to be an equality.
+
+**Evidence 1 — handler-driven invariant, accounting vs. custody.** The handler owns
+three funded, approved actors with bounded inputs; the revert rate is 0, so the
+sequences reached real states:
+
+```
+$ forge test --match-path 'test/audit/SolvencyInvariant.t.sol'
+No files changed, compilation skipped
+
+Ran 1 test for test/audit/SolvencyInvariant.t.sol:SolvencyInvariantTest
+[FAIL: totalAssetsStored drifted from the aUSDT the vault actually holds: 383503204535 != 383510269637]
